From e48f7e57d25b90796801487500b4053b07f05fcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:49:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 144/144] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: exclude the ADSP remote
 heap from Linux RAM

FastRPC assigns the complete ADSP remote heap to DSP VMIDs without taking it out of the CMA allocator. A reusable pool allows normal movable Linux pages to enter memory that HLOS can no longer access.

On OnePlus 13, the old boot log reserves 0xf2c00000..0xf37fffff as reusable ADSP heap. The first clear_page external abort records PFN 0xf3400, inside that region. Six such aborts precede the recorded shutdown/display hang. Mark the heap no-map rather than suppressing memory initialization or IRQ errors. This fixes the demonstrated memory ownership fault; a separate DPU shutdown defect still needs clean-kernel validation.

Link: https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/10/14/2096
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
index 20dc148c71..5a9f06881f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -570,7 +570,7 @@ adsp_rpc_remote_heap_mem: adsp-rpc-remote-heap {
 			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x00000000 0x0 0xffffffff>;
 			alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
 			size = <0x0 0xc00000>;
-			reusable;
+			no-map;
 		};
 	};
 
